"text": "**The gates:** - the new script's tests; - the workflow and leg-script tests; - the audit leg, whose verdict and yanked warning move; - the pre-push gate (`fast`), which now builds skia from the verified file on the dev host; - a witness that the dev host's skia-bindings build read the `file://` URL; - the stand's adapter probe after the lock move; - the evidence count; - the five archives fetched and verified on this host by the script itself, and the count of their measured lines,   all before any CI run."
},
{
"from": 198,
"to": 202,
"text": "**What is not run:** - No Rust source changes, so no new Rust test, no `doc` leg (no doc comment moves) and no `stand-repeat`. `fast`   runs the workspace tests under the new environment. - No boot path or binary start changes, so no smoke entry. - There is no live leg, and the cold-agent pipe is not run."
},
