"prose": [
{
"from": 187,
"to": 196,
"text": "**The gates:** - the new script's tests; - the workflow and leg-script tests; - the audit leg, whose verdict and yanked warning move; - the pre-push gate (`fast`), which now builds skia from the verified file on the dev host; - a witness that the dev host's skia-bindings build read the `file://` URL; - the stand's adapter probe after the lock move; - the evidence count; - the five archives fetched and verified on this host by the script itself, and the count of their measured lines,   all before any CI run."
},
{
"from": 198,
"to": 202,
"text": "**What is not run:** - No Rust source changes, so no new Rust test, no `doc` leg (no doc comment moves) and no `stand-repeat`. `fast`   runs the workspace tests under the new environment. - No boot path or binary start changes, so no smoke entry. - There is no live leg, and the cold-agent pipe is not run."
},
{
"from": 204,
"to": 209,
"text": "**Controls.** After the gates are green, /implement makes two one-shot `gate.py control` runs, never entries. Each is fired with `--timeout 600`, the unittest files running in seconds; a `timeout` reading is not read as held. - **The sum unchecked.** In `skia_archive.py`, remove the sha256 comparison that guards the rename. Fired on gate 1,   case `test_a_mismatched_archive_is_refused` (named by its method). - **The fallback left open.** In `ci-leg.sh`, remove the `FORCE_SKIA_BINARIES_DOWNLOAD=1` export. Fired on gate 2,   case `test_skia_legs_build_from_the_verified_archive`."
},
{
"from": 211,
"to": 214,
"text": "**The diff is OS-sensitive:** - the matrix step picks `python` on windows-latest and `python3` elsewhere; - the printed URL carries a Windows drive path on windows; - each platform builds from its own archive on its own runner (each key and sum measured on this host at step 4)."
},
{
"from": 216,
"to": 216,
"text": "The `ci.py` entry's `note` names the OS leg that witnesses each case."
},
{
"from": 218,
"to": 219,
"text": "**The gated criterion.** The last entry reads the Epoch 2 boundary audit's metric row for `v040-08`. It runs only once its block reads cleared (`--void {n}:block cleared — {evidence}`)."
}
],
